{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399945-which-animal-features-do-you-usually-pick-when-playing-a-gangrel","id":1399945,"title":"Which animal features do you usually pick when playing a Gangrel?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-29T17:02:10-07:00","id":1399945,"title":"Which animal features do you usually pick when playing a Gangrel?","content":"What features did you pick when playing a Gangrel who has frenzied?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T19:03:51-07:00","id":1399972,"title":"","content":"I go all over the place, they just need to be features of indigenous predators. Broad definition of both those terms though. Omnivores and insectivores are predators too. Wolves and bears are still indigenous to an area where they went extinct in relatively recent history. I remember an NPC who as permanent features had rat claws and tail, patches of toad skin and 8 spider eyes. The clanbook said that Gangrel who only exhibit the features of a single species are rare. A guide-line that I like, makes them more monstrous and unnatural.<br /> I guess I haven't focused much on mental features cause I'm scared it'll just get silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T19:28:59-07:00","id":1399976,"title":"","content":"My gaming group and I only picked features of one animal with the notion in our minds that eventually the vampire would turn into that animal if she had enough frenzies over the centuries. It was always a wolf although I think we all would have been fine if someone picked another animal that was iconic to vampires. A bat would probably have been fine - based on the costume makeup of the man-bat hybrid of Gary Oldman in '92's Dracula. Rats could also have been accepted. But I only remember wolves. If a character would have been from a homeland that did not have wolves, but had some other major predator species - like a leopard or jaguar - we would have accepted that. If someone had ever suggested another animal, I think we would have discussed it first to make sure everyone thought it was &quot;appropriate.&quot; We were a fairly traditional group in our tastes.<br /> <br /> The first features were always something noticeable, but not too noticeable so we could operate while leaving the Masquerade intact. That usually meant tufts of fur somewhere on the hair line, or at wrists or elbows. Fingernails and toenails that turned into claws. Teeth that turned into wolf fangs. The type of things that one could draw on a profile picture and still made it look &quot;cool&quot;. After those slots were filled, we typically started picking things that could be covered up and not usually noticed - changes regarding our torso, the start of any possible tail at the bottom of our spine, feet/legs that gradually turned digitirade, large discoloration of skin, etc. At some point someone always picked having wolf eyes.<br /> <br /> The main question we had is how significant the changes had to be, and the answer was always as long as it seemed to match the decline in Appearance mechanically after so many frenzies, it was whatever we wanted. Other than aesthetics, it wasn't going to affect the character or game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T20:46:01-07:00","id":1399984,"title":"","content":"Pointed ears, eyes that shine in bright light to start. I don't go for the chimera thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T21:39:54-07:00","id":1400000,"title":"","content":"Random. Based on common species in the region. Quoll fur. Spiders eyes. Snakes toungue. Crocodile scales. Flying fox pelt. Goanna claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T23:49:55-07:00","id":1400019,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the pointy ears and bright eyes are excessively comfortable. My reference to an elder who has changed during long centuries is Enkidu, who is more chimera or animal than man. In the long term, the Gangrel became monsters, as the Nosferatu. Anyway, there is room for all kind of players and interpretations. If I would roleplay a Gangrel, I would have monkey features.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T02:53:46-07:00","id":1400033,"title":"","content":"I think you're supposed to <i>not</i> have a say. You are not supposed to turn into your spirit animal, you're supposed to turn into a chimerical monster. Turning into an animal you like cheapens that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T03:05:42-07:00","id":1400036,"title":"","content":"Cat ears ^_^ or owl feathers (this is what I would choose, I never actually ran a Gangrel PC)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:35:24-07:00","id":1400097,"title":"","content":"I have a short list I try to get ST approval on. Some editions do say \u201cplayer chooses\u201d so I try to keep as much control over my character\u2019s fate as possible.<br /> <br /> spots, stripes, pelt/fur, alopecia and/or scales on head, chest, abdomen, back, arms, and/or legs (feathers aren't my thing, but possibly)<br /> elongated vertebrae<br /> elongated forearms and/or shins<br /> black lips and/or gums<br /> involuntary growling during stress<br /> mane (lion)<br /> mane (horse)<br /> licking things and/or people I like<br /> ridgeback<br /> enlarged irises<br /> constant sniffing<br /> moist nose<br /> tufted ears<br /> nictitating membranes<br /> additional nipples along abdomen<br /> scuffing/stamping feet in doorways or when agitated<br /> the ability to shed hair (voluntary or not)<br /> webbed toes and/or fingers<br /> impulsive/compulsive chewing of objects<br /> pointed teeth<br /> prominent canines<br /> luminescent eyes<br /> claws<br /> dew claws/four toed feet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:40:59-07:00","id":1400099,"title":"","content":"I had a Gangrel that developed lupine hind legs. He walked on toes/ball of foot, with ankle up in the air, making his legs look disjointed. He had no problem walking normally, but was a giant masquerade breach. The special boots that he had made for him imposed a dex penalty for running, but kept him blending in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T13:46:58-07:00","id":1400172,"title":"","content":"I tend to give them a vague &quot;wild look&quot;, a feral glint in the eyes, a tendency to bare their teeth, threatening body language - something I have a lot of Kindred do, they just tend to do it a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T17:08:18-07:00","id":1400209,"title":"","content":"I usually keep them to a single animal that the character has some sort of connection with on some level or another. Usually starting with the adaption of certain animalistic behaviors, changes to eyes and teeth, then nails, hair, ears, nose, patches of skin. This usually works out to at least a dozen steps, sometimes more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:22:31-07:00","id":1400643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399945-which-animal-features-do-you-usually-pick-when-playing-a-gangrel?p=1400033#post1400033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're supposed to <i>not</i> have a say. You are not supposed to turn into your spirit animal, you're supposed to turn into a chimerical monster. Turning into an animal you like cheapens that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have a point with that, but on the other hand, NPCs seem not to follow the same logic at times. Odin the All-High is positively ancient, for example, but he doesn't look like he gained a lot of animal traits. Which makes even less sense since he keeps eating Garou whenever he's awake and that alone should make him a quivering rageball.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T00:58:53-07:00","id":1400660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399945-which-animal-features-do-you-usually-pick-when-playing-a-gangrel?p=1400643#post1400643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odin the All-High is positively ancient, for example, but he doesn't look like he gained a lot of animal traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is mostly a case of the writers not bothering to think about consequences. It's like how many NPCs's Humanity ratings don't seem to reflect their descriptions. Or how a werewolf's Rage and the associated Curse don't reflect their involvement with ordinary people. Not giving thought to the Gangrel weakness is one of those - except for a few characters where the writer emphasized that trait.<br /> <br /> At some point you just go, &quot;OK, the writer doesn't know what he's doing. Here's what I'm going to do...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:15:25-07:00","id":1400700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399945-which-animal-features-do-you-usually-pick-when-playing-a-gangrel?p=1400660#post1400660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is mostly a case of the writers not bothering to think about consequences. It's like how many NPCs's Humanity ratings don't seem to reflect their descriptions. Or how a werewolf's Rage and the associated Curse don't reflect their involvement with ordinary people. Not giving thought to the Gangrel weakness is one of those - except for a few characters where the writer emphasized that trait.<br /> <br /> At some point you just go, &quot;OK, the writer doesn't know what he's doing. Here's what I'm going to do...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sounds about right.<br /> <br /> I've come across at least one Storyteller who took the decision away from his players. Said he was tired of them picking &quot;cool&quot; features, like cat eyes, wolf ears and so forth. Instead, he took pleasure in handing out things like pig tails and donkey teeth. Not sure I really liked the approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:49:00-07:00","id":1400722,"title":"","content":"I think the player shouldn't get a choice. However, these are some common sense rules so you don't look like a prick giving out &quot;pig tails and donkey teeth&quot;<br /> <br /> -No herbivores. <br /> -No domesticated animals<br /> -Aquatic animals only if the vampire spends good time in the water.<br /> -Exotic creatures the Gangrel has never come into contact with are to be avoided. Animals within a 10km radius of where the the Gangrel has been recently are preferable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:02:07-07:00","id":1400753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399945-which-animal-features-do-you-usually-pick-when-playing-a-gangrel?p=1400722#post1400722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the player shouldn't get a choice. However, these are some common sense rules so you don't look like a prick giving out &quot;pig tails and donkey teeth&quot;<br /> <br /> -No herbivores.<br /> -No domesticated animals<br /> -Aquatic animals only if the vampire spends good time in the water.<br /> -Exotic creatures the Gangrel has never come into contact with are to be avoided. Animals within a 10km radius of where the the Gangrel has been recently are preferable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sound approach!<br /> <br /> If I were to play an Elder Gangrel (or a really unlucky younger one), there's a high chance they'd look like Dwight Renfield. Or one of the Strigos from Warhammer. I admit, I have a type... should not come as a surprise, considering my forum avatar. Though becoming more and more like a stunted Crinos could also be interesting, even if that's going to paint a target on your back from all the insulted Lupines around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T17:04:39-07:00","id":1401018,"title":"","content":"So, from a chronicle I was in many years ago that was set in Miami, one person was playing a Gangrel who had been (and still moonlighted as) a skip tracer and bail bond enforcer. He was fairly notorious even when alive for being incredibly ruthless and tenacious, relentlessly and cold bloodedly hunting down his prey, in a sort of &quot;ambush predator&quot; style. And this carried over into his unlife as a vampire. The player and the ST agreed that it would be interesting to have him develop alligator and reptilian features. This initially started fairly slowly, with a compulsive habit of swallowing rocks and tending to sit very, very still (usually with his mouth slightly open), as well as making this reptilian hissing noise when challenging others and preferring to drown his prey in rapid ambush attacks. He also started losing his hair, eventually being totally hairless. As this progressed, he developed alligator looking eyes, alligator teeth, fingernails that were functionally alligator claws, and rough leathery skin, as well as the compulsion to sleep submerged in water (usually bath tubs) full of murky water with just his nose above the surface. (This wasn't to breath, just to smell potential intruders/prey.) All together, this was considered to be about 7 or 8 total &quot;features&quot; IIRC, which had largely been worked out together between the two of them when the character was being created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T09:00:41-07:00","id":1401131,"title":"","content":"Sounds amazing!<br /> <br /> Heh, I don't even remember anyone ever playing a Gangrel at our table, come to think of it. Brujah, Tremere... Lasombra Antis, Setites, sometimes a Malkavian (me), a Nosferatu (also me)... we usually had a number of female players, and they never went for any of the 'ugly' clans.<br /> <br /> One guy always wanted to play a Gargoyle, but he never got to. STs around here didn't like the bloodline very much. Maybe he should've made a Gangrel and have him develop in that direction instead? Sure, he won't be able to fly, but that's not what he wanted anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T11:52:13-07:00","id":1401158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399945-which-animal-features-do-you-usually-pick-when-playing-a-gangrel?p=1401131#post1401131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds amazing!<br /> <br /> Heh, I don't even remember anyone ever playing a Gangrel at our table, come to think of it. Brujah, Tremere... Lasombra Antis, Setites, sometimes a Malkavian (me), a Nosferatu (also me)... we usually had a number of female players, and they never went for any of the 'ugly' clans.<br /> <br /> One guy always wanted to play a Gargoyle, but he never got to. STs around here didn't like the bloodline very much. Maybe he should've made a Gangrel and have him develop in that direction instead? Sure, he won't be able to fly, but that's not what he wanted anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I noticed that, too. I currently play with three females. Two play Toreadors, one plays a Malkavian. All three have the looks merit.<br /> I'm playing a Gangrel in a game. I've only frenzied once, but the ST let me pick, so I went with predatory bird hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T12:37:50-07:00","id":1401170,"title":"","content":"I did once see a female Gangrel player who had based her character on the East Asian &quot;fox woman&quot; concept (kitsune/gumiho/juiweihu). It was pretty cool, especially because she could mimic that barking laugh thing that foxes do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}